## Control {{controlId}}: Check Media Containing Diagnostic and Test Programs for Malicious Code Before Use

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization checks maintenance media for malicious code within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Microsoft Defender for Endpoint scanning and device compliance policies managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Access Control for Maintenance Sessions:**
{{caPoliciesTotalCount}} Conditional Access policies require MFA and compliant device status for non-local maintenance sessions:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/each}}

Remote maintenance sessions are authenticated via MFA, encrypted via TLS 1.2+, and automatically terminated when maintenance is complete through session timeout controls.
{{else}}
Conditional Access enforcement for maintenance sessions has not been configured.
{{/if}}

**Malicious Code Detection:**
- Microsoft Defender for Endpoint provides real-time scanning of all media connected to managed devices
- Diagnostic tools downloaded from external sources are scanned before execution
- PowerShell scripts used for maintenance must be signed with approved certificates
- Removable media containing maintenance tools scanned automatically upon connection

{{#if compliancePolicyActive}}
**Compliance Enforcement:**
Device compliance policy "{{policyName}}" requires active antivirus protection and real-time scanning, ensuring maintenance media is checked before use on CUI systems.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Defender for Endpoint scan logs, maintenance media inspection records, script signing policies, and compliance policy configurations.

